From b11c67307f595579b8c0c588c96ccfc02358bccf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:49:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(front): decline only where the spec names the
 operator TLC's Java class replaces

The check of a module of the user's named after one of TLC's own
classes matched a reference by the last part of the name as written,
so a root definition spelled like the replaced operator declined a
model main checks (I == INSTANCE TransitiveClosure, Warshall(a) == a).
It now finds the definitions TLC replaces, and their copies an
INSTANCE makes, by their place in their module, and declines only where
an expression of the spec or the configuration resolves to one of
them: through EXTENDS, a named or LOCAL INSTANCE, or a substitution of
the configuration, and not through an operator another module spells
the same.
